These counts measure reported service-affecting incidents, not organisation-level attack probabilities. The report notes changes in coverage, including over-the-top services. A 2025 observation was not established in the retrieved annual series. ([enisa.europa.eu](https://www.enisa.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2025-07/ENISA_Telecom_Security_Incidents_2024_en.pdf))

For 2024, the report records 113 system-failure incidents, 35 human-error incidents, 25 natural-phenomena incidents and 15 malicious-action incidents. “Malicious action” is not synonymous with ransomware. The report’s executive summary and root-cause section also give different participating-country counts, limiting precision about geographic coverage. ([enisa.europa.eu](https://www.enisa.europa.eu/sites/default/files/2025-07/ENISA_Telecom_Security_Incidents_2024_en.pdf))



