Ofcom links much of the resilience-report reduction to the transition from copper telephony to fibre-enabled voice services. It should not be interpreted as an equivalent reduction in cyber exposure. Confidence: High for the reported counts; Medium for broader trend interpretation. ([gov.uk](https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ofcom-security-report-for-the-period-october-2024-to-october-2025/ofcom-security-report-for-the-period-october-2024-to-october-2025))




**Ransomware gap:** A consistent five-year telecom-only ransomware series meeting the requested source and metadata standard was not established. No all-sector ransomware percentage has been inserted as a telecom value.

**Normalisation:** Neither series supplies the complete, stable operator/customer/revenue denominator needed for a cross-sector incident rate. Mandatory reporting thresholds, changing coverage and incident definitions prevent direct comparison with voluntary breach-investigation datasets.


